11:     - Several smaller colored sprites scattered around the bar.
12: 
13:     Rule:
14:     - Each bar notch is filled by a root piece whose shape exactly covers the hole.
15:     - The root defines a strip (column-span or row-span) for its chain.
16:     - Successive pieces fill the bg cells inside the previous piece's bbox, locked to the same strip width.
17:     - Multiple chains grow independently from different bar notches.
18: 
19:     Key insight: The root piece's extent perpendicular to the chain direction locks the strip width for all subsequent pieces in that chain.
20:     """
